---
title: Not Found Errors
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ This page covers the newer "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" API for handling not found errors. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" route is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. See "},{"type":"link","href":"#migrating-from-notfoundroute","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Overview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are 2 uses for not-found errors in TanStack Router:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Non-matching route paths"}]},{"type":"text","value":": When a path does not match any known route matching pattern "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OR"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when it partially matches a route, but with extra path segments"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"router"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will automatically throw a not-found error when a path does not match any known route matching pattern"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the router's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fuzzy"},{"type":"text","value":", the nearest matching route with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" will handle the error. If the router's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"root"},{"type":"text","value":", the root route will handle the error."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attempting to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/users"},{"type":"text","value":" when there is no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/users"},{"type":"text","value":" route"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attempting to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/1/edit"},{"type":"text","value":" when the route tree only handles "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/$postId"}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing resources"}]},{"type":"text","value":": When a resource cannot be found, such as a post with a given ID or any asynchronous data that is not available or does not exist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You, the developer"}]},{"type":"text","value":" must throw a not-found error when a resource cannot be found. This can be done in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":" functions using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" utility."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Will be handled by the nearest matching route with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" (when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" is called within "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loader"},{"type":"text","value":") or the root route."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attempting to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/1"},{"type":"text","value":" when the post with ID 1 does not exist"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attempting to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/docs/path/to/document"},{"type":"text","value":" when the document does not exist"}]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood, both of these cases are implemented using the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" API."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-notfoundmode-option","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" option"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When TanStack Router encounters a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"pathname"}]},{"type":"text","value":" that doesn't match any known route pattern "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OR"}]},{"type":"text","value":" partially matches a route pattern but with extra trailing pathname segments, it will automatically throw a not-found error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depending on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" option, the router will handle these automatic errors differently:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#notfoundmode-fuzzy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"fuzzy\" mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (default): The router will intelligently find the closest matching suitable route and display the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#notfoundmode-root","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\"root\" mode"}]},{"type":"text","value":": All not-found errors will be handled by the root route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", regardless of the nearest matching route."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"notfoundmode-fuzzy","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode: 'fuzzy'"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the router's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fuzzy"},{"type":"text","value":", which indicates that if a pathname doesn't match any known route, the router will attempt to use the closest matching route with a configured "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"❓ Why is this the default?"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Fuzzy matching to preserve as much parent layout as possible for the user gives them more context to navigate to a useful location based on where they thought they would arrive."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The nearest suitable route is found using the following criteria:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The route must have a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured or the router must have a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultNotFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, consider the following route tree:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__root__"},{"type":"text","value":" (has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts"},{"type":"text","value":" (has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$postId"},{"type":"text","value":" (has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured)"}]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided the path of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/1/edit"},{"type":"text","value":", the following component structure will be rendered:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Root>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Posts>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Post>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Post.notFoundComponent>"}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$postId"},{"type":"text","value":" route will be rendered because it is the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"nearest matching route with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"notfoundmode-root","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode: 'root'"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"root"},{"type":"text","value":", all not-found errors will be handled by the root route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of bubbling up from the nearest fuzzy-matched route."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, consider the following route tree:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__root__"},{"type":"text","value":" (has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"posts"},{"type":"text","value":" (has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured)"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$postId"},{"type":"text","value":" (has a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" configured)"}]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If provided the path of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/1/edit"},{"type":"text","value":", the following component structure will be rendered:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Root>"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Root.notFoundComponent>"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" of the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"__root__"},{"type":"text","value":" route will be rendered because the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"root"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuring-a-route-s-notfoundcomponent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuring a route's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To handle both types of not-found errors, you can attach a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" to a route. This component will be rendered when a not-found error is thrown."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, configuring a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" for a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/settings"},{"type":"text","value":" route to handle non-existing settings pages:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/settings')({\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Settings page</p>\n        <Outlet />\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>This setting page doesn't exist!</p>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Or configuring a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" for a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/posts/$postId"},{"type":"text","value":" route to handle posts that don't exist:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) throw notFound()\n    return { post }\n  },\n  component: ({ post }) => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n        <p>{post.body}</p>\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Post not found!</p>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-router-wide-not-found-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default Router-Wide Not Found Handling"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You may want to provide a default not-found component for every route in your app with child routes."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why only routes with children? "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Leaf-node routes (routes without children) will never render an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Outlet"},{"type":"text","value":" and therefore are not able to handle not-found errors."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To do this, pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultNotFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createRouter"},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const router = createRouter({\n  defaultNotFoundComponent: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Not found!</p>\n        <Link to=\"/\">Go home</Link>\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"throwing-your-own-notfound-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throwing your own "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can manually throw not-found errors in loader methods and components using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function. This is useful when you need to signal that a resource cannot be found."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function works in a similar fashion to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"redirect"},{"type":"text","value":" function. To cause a not-found error, you can "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"throw a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    // Returns `null` if the post doesn't exist\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) {\n      throw notFound()\n      // Alternatively, you can make the notFound function throw:\n      // notFound({ throw: true })\n    }\n    // Post is guaranteed to be defined here because we threw an error\n    return { post }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The not-found error above will be handled by the same route or nearest parent route that has either a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" route option or the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultNotFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" router option configured."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If neither the route nor any suitable parent route is found to handle the error, the root route will handle it using TanStack Router's "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extremely basic (and purposefully undesirable)"}]},{"type":"text","value":" default not-found component that simply renders "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<p>Not Found</p>"},{"type":"text","value":". It's highly recommended to either attach at least one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" to the root route or configure a router-wide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultNotFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" to handle not-found errors."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ When you throw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound()"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":", TanStack Router resolves it the same way as other not-found errors:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routeId"},{"type":"text","value":", that route (or the nearest valid ancestor boundary) handles it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you don't pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"routeId"},{"type":"text","value":", the nearest route/ancestor with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" handles it (based on the router's mode and matching rules)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If no suitable boundary is found, handling falls back to the root/default not-found behavior."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"beforeLoad"},{"type":"text","value":"-thrown not-found errors, TanStack Router still runs required parent loaders so the selected not-found boundary can render with the loader data it depends on."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"specifying-which-routes-handle-not-found-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specifying Which Routes Handle Not Found Errors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sometimes you may want to trigger a not-found on a specific parent route and bypass the normal not-found component propagation. To do this, pass in a route id to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"route"},{"type":"text","value":" option in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// _pathlessLayout.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_pathlessLayout')({\n  // This will render\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Not found (in _pathlessLayout)</p>\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>This is a pathless layout route!</p>\n        <Outlet />\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n\n// _pathlessLayout/route-a.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_pathless/route-a')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // This will make LayoutRoute handle the not-found error\n    throw notFound({ routeId: '/_pathlessLayout' })\n    //                      ^^^^^^^^^ This will autocomplete from the registered router\n  },\n  // This WILL NOT render\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Not found (in _pathlessLayout/route-a)</p>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"manually-targeting-the-root-route","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manually targeting the root route"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also target the root route by passing the exported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"rootRouteId"},{"type":"text","value":" variable to the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"route"},{"type":"text","value":" property:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) throw notFound({ routeId: rootRouteId })\n    return { post }\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"throwing-not-found-errors-in-components","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throwing Not Found Errors in Components"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also throw not-found errors in components. However, "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"it is recommended to throw not-found errors in loader methods instead of components in order to correctly type loader data and prevent flickering."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Router exposes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CatchNotFound"},{"type":"text","value":" component similar to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CatchBoundary"},{"type":"text","value":" that can be used to catch not-found errors in components and display UI accordingly."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"data-loading-inside-notfoundcomponent","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Data Loading Inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" is a special case when it comes to data loading. "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SomeRoute.useLoaderData"},{"type":"text","value":" may not be defined depending on which route you are trying to access and where the not-found error gets thrown"}]},{"type":"text","value":". However, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route.useParams"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route.useSearch"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Route.useRouteContext"},{"type":"text","value":", etc. will return a defined value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need to pass incomplete loader data to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":","}]},{"type":"text","value":" pass the data via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" option in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function and validate it in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"export const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post)\n      throw notFound({\n        // Forward some data to the notFoundComponent\n        // data: someIncompleteLoaderData\n      })\n    return { post }\n  },\n  // `data: unknown` is passed to the component via the `data` option when calling `notFound`\n  notFoundComponent: ({ data }) => {\n    // ❌ useLoaderData is not valid here: const { post } = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n    // ✅:\n    const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n    const search = Route.useSearch()\n    const context = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n    return <p>Post with id {postId} not found!</p>\n  },\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usage-with-ssr","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Usage With SSR"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"./ssr.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSR guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more information."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"migrating-from-notfoundroute","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" API is deprecated in favor of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" API will be removed in a future release."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFound"},{"type":"text","value":" function and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" will not work when using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main differences are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" is a route that requires an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet>"},{"type":"text","value":" on its parent route to render. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" is a component that can be attached to any route."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":", you can't use layouts. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" can be used with layouts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", path matching is strict. This means that if you have a route at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/post/$postId"},{"type":"text","value":", a not-found error will be thrown if you try to access "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/post/1/2/3"},{"type":"text","value":". With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/post/1/2/3"},{"type":"text","value":" would match the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" and only render it if there is an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To migrate from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NotFoundRoute"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":", you'll just need to make a few changes:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen.'\n- import { notFoundRoute } from './notFoundRoute'  // [!code --]\n\nexport const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n- notFoundRoute // [!code --]\n})\n\n// routes/__root.tsx\nimport { createRootRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  // ...\n+ notFoundComponent: () => {  // [!code ++]\n+   return <p>Not found!</p>  // [!code ++]\n+ } // [!code ++]\n})","lang":"tsx","meta":"title='src/router.tsx'","title":"src/router.tsx","file":"src/router.tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Important changes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" is added to the root route for global not-found handling."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also add a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" to any other route in your route tree to handle not-found errors for that specific route."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"notFoundComponent"},{"type":"text","value":" does not support rendering an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Outlet>"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"id":"the-notfoundmode-option","text":"The notFoundMode option","level":2},{"id":"notfoundmode-fuzzy","text":"notFoundMode: 'fuzzy'","level":3},{"id":"notfoundmode-root","text":"notFoundMode: 'root'","level":3},{"id":"configuring-a-route-s-notfoundcomponent","text":"Configuring a route's notFoundComponent","level":2},{"id":"default-router-wide-not-found-handling","text":"Default Router-Wide Not Found Handling","level":2},{"id":"throwing-your-own-notfound-errors","text":"Throwing your own notFound errors","level":2},{"id":"specifying-which-routes-handle-not-found-errors","text":"Specifying Which Routes Handle Not Found Errors","level":2},{"id":"manually-targeting-the-root-route","text":"Manually targeting the root route","level":3},{"id":"throwing-not-found-errors-in-components","text":"Throwing Not Found Errors in Components","level":3},{"id":"data-loading-inside-notfoundcomponent","text":"Data Loading Inside notFoundComponent","level":3},{"id":"usage-with-ssr","text":"Usage With SSR","level":2},{"id":"migrating-from-notfoundroute","text":"Migrating from NotFoundRoute","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> ⚠️ This page covers the newer `notFound` function and `notFoundComponent` API for handling not found errors. The `NotFoundRoute` route is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. See [Migrating from `NotFoundRoute`](#migrating-from-notfoundroute) for more information.\n\n## Overview\n\nThere are 2 uses for not-found errors in TanStack Router:\n\n- **Non-matching route paths**: When a path does not match any known route matching pattern **OR** when it partially matches a route, but with extra path segments\n  - The **router** will automatically throw a not-found error when a path does not match any known route matching pattern\n  - If the router's `notFoundMode` is set to `fuzzy`, the nearest matching route with a `notFoundComponent` will handle the error. If the router's `notFoundMode` is set to `root`, the root route will handle the error.\n  - Examples:\n    - Attempting to access `/users` when there is no `/users` route\n    - Attempting to access `/posts/1/edit` when the route tree only handles `/posts/$postId`\n- **Missing resources**: When a resource cannot be found, such as a post with a given ID or any asynchronous data that is not available or does not exist\n  - **You, the developer** must throw a not-found error when a resource cannot be found. This can be done in the `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions using the `notFound` utility.\n  - Will be handled by the nearest matching route with a `notFoundComponent` (when `notFound` is called within `loader`) or the root route.\n  - Examples:\n    - Attempting to access `/posts/1` when the post with ID 1 does not exist\n    - Attempting to access `/docs/path/to/document` when the document does not exist\n\nUnder the hood, both of these cases are implemented using the same `notFound` function and `notFoundComponent` API.\n\n## The `notFoundMode` option\n\nWhen TanStack Router encounters a **pathname** that doesn't match any known route pattern **OR** partially matches a route pattern but with extra trailing pathname segments, it will automatically throw a not-found error.\n\nDepending on the `notFoundMode` option, the router will handle these automatic errors differently:\n\n- [\"fuzzy\" mode](#notfoundmode-fuzzy) (default): The router will intelligently find the closest matching suitable route and display the `notFoundComponent`.\n- [\"root\" mode](#notfoundmode-root): All not-found errors will be handled by the root route's `notFoundComponent`, regardless of the nearest matching route.\n\n### `notFoundMode: 'fuzzy'`\n\nBy default, the router's `notFoundMode` is set to `fuzzy`, which indicates that if a pathname doesn't match any known route, the router will attempt to use the closest matching route with a configured `notFoundComponent`.\n\n> **❓ Why is this the default?** Fuzzy matching to preserve as much parent layout as possible for the user gives them more context to navigate to a useful location based on where they thought they would arrive.\n\nThe nearest suitable route is found using the following criteria:\n\n- The route must have a `notFoundComponent` configured or the router must have a `defaultNotFoundComponent` configured\n\nFor example, consider the following route tree:\n\n- `__root__` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n  - `posts` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n    - `$postId` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n\nIf provided the path of `/posts/1/edit`, the following component structure will be rendered:\n\n- `<Root>`\n  - `<Posts>`\n    - `<Post>`\n      - `<Post.notFoundComponent>`\n\nThe `notFoundComponent` of the `$postId` route will be rendered because it is the **nearest matching route with a `notFoundComponent` configured**.\n\n### `notFoundMode: 'root'`\n\nWhen `notFoundMode` is set to `root`, all not-found errors will be handled by the root route's `notFoundComponent` instead of bubbling up from the nearest fuzzy-matched route.\n\nFor example, consider the following route tree:\n\n- `__root__` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n  - `posts` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n    - `$postId` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n\nIf provided the path of `/posts/1/edit`, the following component structure will be rendered:\n\n- `<Root>`\n  - `<Root.notFoundComponent>`\n\nThe `notFoundComponent` of the `__root__` route will be rendered because the `notFoundMode` is set to `root`.\n\n## Configuring a route's `notFoundComponent`\n\nTo handle both types of not-found errors, you can attach a `notFoundComponent` to a route. This component will be rendered when a not-found error is thrown.\n\nFor example, configuring a `notFoundComponent` for a `/settings` route to handle non-existing settings pages:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/settings')({\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Settings page</p>\n        <Outlet />\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>This setting page doesn't exist!</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOr configuring a `notFoundComponent` for a `/posts/$postId` route to handle posts that don't exist:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) throw notFound()\n    return { post }\n  },\n  component: ({ post }) => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n        <p>{post.body}</p>\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Post not found!</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Default Router-Wide Not Found Handling\n\nYou may want to provide a default not-found component for every route in your app with child routes.\n\n> Why only routes with children? **Leaf-node routes (routes without children) will never render an `Outlet` and therefore are not able to handle not-found errors.**\n\nTo do this, pass a `defaultNotFoundComponent` to the `createRouter` function:\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  defaultNotFoundComponent: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Not found!</p>\n        <Link to=\"/\">Go home</Link>\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Throwing your own `notFound` errors\n\nYou can manually throw not-found errors in loader methods and components using the `notFound` function. This is useful when you need to signal that a resource cannot be found.\n\nThe `notFound` function works in a similar fashion to the `redirect` function. To cause a not-found error, you can **throw a `notFound()`**.\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    // Returns `null` if the post doesn't exist\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) {\n      throw notFound()\n      // Alternatively, you can make the notFound function throw:\n      // notFound({ throw: true })\n    }\n    // Post is guaranteed to be defined here because we threw an error\n    return { post }\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe not-found error above will be handled by the same route or nearest parent route that has either a `notFoundComponent` route option or the `defaultNotFoundComponent` router option configured.\n\nIf neither the route nor any suitable parent route is found to handle the error, the root route will handle it using TanStack Router's **extremely basic (and purposefully undesirable)** default not-found component that simply renders `<p>Not Found</p>`. It's highly recommended to either attach at least one `notFoundComponent` to the root route or configure a router-wide `defaultNotFoundComponent` to handle not-found errors.\n\n> ⚠️ When you throw `notFound()` in `beforeLoad`, TanStack Router resolves it the same way as other not-found errors:\n>\n> - If you pass `routeId`, that route (or the nearest valid ancestor boundary) handles it.\n> - If you don't pass `routeId`, the nearest route/ancestor with a `notFoundComponent` handles it (based on the router's mode and matching rules).\n> - If no suitable boundary is found, handling falls back to the root/default not-found behavior.\n>\n> For `beforeLoad`-thrown not-found errors, TanStack Router still runs required parent loaders so the selected not-found boundary can render with the loader data it depends on.\n\n## Specifying Which Routes Handle Not Found Errors\n\nSometimes you may want to trigger a not-found on a specific parent route and bypass the normal not-found component propagation. To do this, pass in a route id to the `route` option in the `notFound` function.\n\n```tsx\n// _pathlessLayout.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_pathlessLayout')({\n  // This will render\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Not found (in _pathlessLayout)</p>\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>This is a pathless layout route!</p>\n        <Outlet />\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n\n// _pathlessLayout/route-a.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_pathless/route-a')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // This will make LayoutRoute handle the not-found error\n    throw notFound({ routeId: '/_pathlessLayout' })\n    //                      ^^^^^^^^^ This will autocomplete from the registered router\n  },\n  // This WILL NOT render\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Not found (in _pathlessLayout/route-a)</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Manually targeting the root route\n\nYou can also target the root route by passing the exported `rootRouteId` variable to the `notFound` function's `route` property:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) throw notFound({ routeId: rootRouteId })\n    return { post }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Throwing Not Found Errors in Components\n\nYou can also throw not-found errors in components. However, **it is recommended to throw not-found errors in loader methods instead of components in order to correctly type loader data and prevent flickering.**\n\nTanStack Router exposes a `CatchNotFound` component similar to `CatchBoundary` that can be used to catch not-found errors in components and display UI accordingly.\n\n### Data Loading Inside `notFoundComponent`\n\n`notFoundComponent` is a special case when it comes to data loading. **`SomeRoute.useLoaderData` may not be defined depending on which route you are trying to access and where the not-found error gets thrown**. However, `Route.useParams`, `Route.useSearch`, `Route.useRouteContext`, etc. will return a defined value.\n\n**If you need to pass incomplete loader data to `notFoundComponent`,** pass the data via the `data` option in the `notFound` function and validate it in `notFoundComponent`.\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post)\n      throw notFound({\n        // Forward some data to the notFoundComponent\n        // data: someIncompleteLoaderData\n      })\n    return { post }\n  },\n  // `data: unknown` is passed to the component via the `data` option when calling `notFound`\n  notFoundComponent: ({ data }) => {\n    // ❌ useLoaderData is not valid here: const { post } = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n    // ✅:\n    const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n    const search = Route.useSearch()\n    const context = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n    return <p>Post with id {postId} not found!</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Usage With SSR\n\nSee [SSR guide](./ssr.md) for more information.\n\n## Migrating from `NotFoundRoute`\n\nThe `NotFoundRoute` API is deprecated in favor of `notFoundComponent`. The `NotFoundRoute` API will be removed in a future release.\n\n**The `notFound` function and `notFoundComponent` will not work when using `NotFoundRoute`.**\n\nThe main differences are:\n\n- `NotFoundRoute` is a route that requires an `<Outlet>` on its parent route to render. `notFoundComponent` is a component that can be attached to any route.\n- When using `NotFoundRoute`, you can't use layouts. `notFoundComponent` can be used with layouts.\n- When using `notFoundComponent`, path matching is strict. This means that if you have a route at `/post/$postId`, a not-found error will be thrown if you try to access `/post/1/2/3`. With `NotFoundRoute`, `/post/1/2/3` would match the `NotFoundRoute` and only render it if there is an `<Outlet>`.\n\nTo migrate from `NotFoundRoute` to `notFoundComponent`, you'll just need to make a few changes:\n\n```tsx title='src/router.tsx'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen.'\n- import { notFoundRoute } from './notFoundRoute'  // [!code --]\n\nexport const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n- notFoundRoute // [!code --]\n})\n\n// routes/__root.tsx\nimport { createRootRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  // ...\n+ notFoundComponent: () => {  // [!code ++]\n+   return <p>Not found!</p>  // [!code ++]\n+ } // [!code ++]\n})\n```\n\nImportant changes:\n\n- A `notFoundComponent` is added to the root route for global not-found handling.\n  - You can also add a `notFoundComponent` to any other route in your route tree to handle not-found errors for that specific route.\n- The `notFoundComponent` does not support rendering an `<Outlet>`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Not Found Errors\n---\n\n> ⚠️ This page covers the newer `notFound` function and `notFoundComponent` API for handling not found errors. The `NotFoundRoute` route is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. See [Migrating from `NotFoundRoute`](#migrating-from-notfoundroute) for more information.\n\n## Overview\n\nThere are 2 uses for not-found errors in TanStack Router:\n\n- **Non-matching route paths**: When a path does not match any known route matching pattern **OR** when it partially matches a route, but with extra path segments\n  - The **router** will automatically throw a not-found error when a path does not match any known route matching pattern\n  - If the router's `notFoundMode` is set to `fuzzy`, the nearest matching route with a `notFoundComponent` will handle the error. If the router's `notFoundMode` is set to `root`, the root route will handle the error.\n  - Examples:\n    - Attempting to access `/users` when there is no `/users` route\n    - Attempting to access `/posts/1/edit` when the route tree only handles `/posts/$postId`\n- **Missing resources**: When a resource cannot be found, such as a post with a given ID or any asynchronous data that is not available or does not exist\n  - **You, the developer** must throw a not-found error when a resource cannot be found. This can be done in the `beforeLoad` or `loader` functions using the `notFound` utility.\n  - Will be handled by the nearest matching route with a `notFoundComponent` (when `notFound` is called within `loader`) or the root route.\n  - Examples:\n    - Attempting to access `/posts/1` when the post with ID 1 does not exist\n    - Attempting to access `/docs/path/to/document` when the document does not exist\n\nUnder the hood, both of these cases are implemented using the same `notFound` function and `notFoundComponent` API.\n\n## The `notFoundMode` option\n\nWhen TanStack Router encounters a **pathname** that doesn't match any known route pattern **OR** partially matches a route pattern but with extra trailing pathname segments, it will automatically throw a not-found error.\n\nDepending on the `notFoundMode` option, the router will handle these automatic errors differently:\n\n- [\"fuzzy\" mode](#notfoundmode-fuzzy) (default): The router will intelligently find the closest matching suitable route and display the `notFoundComponent`.\n- [\"root\" mode](#notfoundmode-root): All not-found errors will be handled by the root route's `notFoundComponent`, regardless of the nearest matching route.\n\n### `notFoundMode: 'fuzzy'`\n\nBy default, the router's `notFoundMode` is set to `fuzzy`, which indicates that if a pathname doesn't match any known route, the router will attempt to use the closest matching route with a configured `notFoundComponent`.\n\n> **❓ Why is this the default?** Fuzzy matching to preserve as much parent layout as possible for the user gives them more context to navigate to a useful location based on where they thought they would arrive.\n\nThe nearest suitable route is found using the following criteria:\n\n- The route must have a `notFoundComponent` configured or the router must have a `defaultNotFoundComponent` configured\n\nFor example, consider the following route tree:\n\n- `__root__` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n  - `posts` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n    - `$postId` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n\nIf provided the path of `/posts/1/edit`, the following component structure will be rendered:\n\n- `<Root>`\n  - `<Posts>`\n    - `<Post>`\n      - `<Post.notFoundComponent>`\n\nThe `notFoundComponent` of the `$postId` route will be rendered because it is the **nearest matching route with a `notFoundComponent` configured**.\n\n### `notFoundMode: 'root'`\n\nWhen `notFoundMode` is set to `root`, all not-found errors will be handled by the root route's `notFoundComponent` instead of bubbling up from the nearest fuzzy-matched route.\n\nFor example, consider the following route tree:\n\n- `__root__` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n  - `posts` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n    - `$postId` (has a `notFoundComponent` configured)\n\nIf provided the path of `/posts/1/edit`, the following component structure will be rendered:\n\n- `<Root>`\n  - `<Root.notFoundComponent>`\n\nThe `notFoundComponent` of the `__root__` route will be rendered because the `notFoundMode` is set to `root`.\n\n## Configuring a route's `notFoundComponent`\n\nTo handle both types of not-found errors, you can attach a `notFoundComponent` to a route. This component will be rendered when a not-found error is thrown.\n\nFor example, configuring a `notFoundComponent` for a `/settings` route to handle non-existing settings pages:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/settings')({\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Settings page</p>\n        <Outlet />\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>This setting page doesn't exist!</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\nOr configuring a `notFoundComponent` for a `/posts/$postId` route to handle posts that don't exist:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) throw notFound()\n    return { post }\n  },\n  component: ({ post }) => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <h1>{post.title}</h1>\n        <p>{post.body}</p>\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Post not found!</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Default Router-Wide Not Found Handling\n\nYou may want to provide a default not-found component for every route in your app with child routes.\n\n> Why only routes with children? **Leaf-node routes (routes without children) will never render an `Outlet` and therefore are not able to handle not-found errors.**\n\nTo do this, pass a `defaultNotFoundComponent` to the `createRouter` function:\n\n```tsx\nconst router = createRouter({\n  defaultNotFoundComponent: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>Not found!</p>\n        <Link to=\"/\">Go home</Link>\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Throwing your own `notFound` errors\n\nYou can manually throw not-found errors in loader methods and components using the `notFound` function. This is useful when you need to signal that a resource cannot be found.\n\nThe `notFound` function works in a similar fashion to the `redirect` function. To cause a not-found error, you can **throw a `notFound()`**.\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    // Returns `null` if the post doesn't exist\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) {\n      throw notFound()\n      // Alternatively, you can make the notFound function throw:\n      // notFound({ throw: true })\n    }\n    // Post is guaranteed to be defined here because we threw an error\n    return { post }\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe not-found error above will be handled by the same route or nearest parent route that has either a `notFoundComponent` route option or the `defaultNotFoundComponent` router option configured.\n\nIf neither the route nor any suitable parent route is found to handle the error, the root route will handle it using TanStack Router's **extremely basic (and purposefully undesirable)** default not-found component that simply renders `<p>Not Found</p>`. It's highly recommended to either attach at least one `notFoundComponent` to the root route or configure a router-wide `defaultNotFoundComponent` to handle not-found errors.\n\n> ⚠️ When you throw `notFound()` in `beforeLoad`, TanStack Router resolves it the same way as other not-found errors:\n>\n> - If you pass `routeId`, that route (or the nearest valid ancestor boundary) handles it.\n> - If you don't pass `routeId`, the nearest route/ancestor with a `notFoundComponent` handles it (based on the router's mode and matching rules).\n> - If no suitable boundary is found, handling falls back to the root/default not-found behavior.\n>\n> For `beforeLoad`-thrown not-found errors, TanStack Router still runs required parent loaders so the selected not-found boundary can render with the loader data it depends on.\n\n## Specifying Which Routes Handle Not Found Errors\n\nSometimes you may want to trigger a not-found on a specific parent route and bypass the normal not-found component propagation. To do this, pass in a route id to the `route` option in the `notFound` function.\n\n```tsx\n// _pathlessLayout.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_pathlessLayout')({\n  // This will render\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Not found (in _pathlessLayout)</p>\n  },\n  component: () => {\n    return (\n      <div>\n        <p>This is a pathless layout route!</p>\n        <Outlet />\n      </div>\n    )\n  },\n})\n\n// _pathlessLayout/route-a.tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/_pathless/route-a')({\n  loader: async () => {\n    // This will make LayoutRoute handle the not-found error\n    throw notFound({ routeId: '/_pathlessLayout' })\n    //                      ^^^^^^^^^ This will autocomplete from the registered router\n  },\n  // This WILL NOT render\n  notFoundComponent: () => {\n    return <p>Not found (in _pathlessLayout/route-a)</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Manually targeting the root route\n\nYou can also target the root route by passing the exported `rootRouteId` variable to the `notFound` function's `route` property:\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post) throw notFound({ routeId: rootRouteId })\n    return { post }\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### Throwing Not Found Errors in Components\n\nYou can also throw not-found errors in components. However, **it is recommended to throw not-found errors in loader methods instead of components in order to correctly type loader data and prevent flickering.**\n\nTanStack Router exposes a `CatchNotFound` component similar to `CatchBoundary` that can be used to catch not-found errors in components and display UI accordingly.\n\n### Data Loading Inside `notFoundComponent`\n\n`notFoundComponent` is a special case when it comes to data loading. **`SomeRoute.useLoaderData` may not be defined depending on which route you are trying to access and where the not-found error gets thrown**. However, `Route.useParams`, `Route.useSearch`, `Route.useRouteContext`, etc. will return a defined value.\n\n**If you need to pass incomplete loader data to `notFoundComponent`,** pass the data via the `data` option in the `notFound` function and validate it in `notFoundComponent`.\n\n```tsx\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/posts/$postId')({\n  loader: async ({ params: { postId } }) => {\n    const post = await getPost(postId)\n    if (!post)\n      throw notFound({\n        // Forward some data to the notFoundComponent\n        // data: someIncompleteLoaderData\n      })\n    return { post }\n  },\n  // `data: unknown` is passed to the component via the `data` option when calling `notFound`\n  notFoundComponent: ({ data }) => {\n    // ❌ useLoaderData is not valid here: const { post } = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n    // ✅:\n    const { postId } = Route.useParams()\n    const search = Route.useSearch()\n    const context = Route.useRouteContext()\n\n    return <p>Post with id {postId} not found!</p>\n  },\n})\n```\n\n## Usage With SSR\n\nSee [SSR guide](./ssr.md) for more information.\n\n## Migrating from `NotFoundRoute`\n\nThe `NotFoundRoute` API is deprecated in favor of `notFoundComponent`. The `NotFoundRoute` API will be removed in a future release.\n\n**The `notFound` function and `notFoundComponent` will not work when using `NotFoundRoute`.**\n\nThe main differences are:\n\n- `NotFoundRoute` is a route that requires an `<Outlet>` on its parent route to render. `notFoundComponent` is a component that can be attached to any route.\n- When using `NotFoundRoute`, you can't use layouts. `notFoundComponent` can be used with layouts.\n- When using `notFoundComponent`, path matching is strict. This means that if you have a route at `/post/$postId`, a not-found error will be thrown if you try to access `/post/1/2/3`. With `NotFoundRoute`, `/post/1/2/3` would match the `NotFoundRoute` and only render it if there is an `<Outlet>`.\n\nTo migrate from `NotFoundRoute` to `notFoundComponent`, you'll just need to make a few changes:\n\n```tsx title='src/router.tsx'\nimport { createRouter } from '@tanstack/react-router'\nimport { routeTree } from './routeTree.gen.'\n- import { notFoundRoute } from './notFoundRoute'  // [!code --]\n\nexport const router = createRouter({\n  routeTree,\n- notFoundRoute // [!code --]\n})\n\n// routes/__root.tsx\nimport { createRootRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nexport const Route = createRootRoute({\n  // ...\n+ notFoundComponent: () => {  // [!code ++]\n+   return <p>Not found!</p>  // [!code ++]\n+ } // [!code ++]\n})\n```\n\nImportant changes:\n\n- A `notFoundComponent` is added to the root route for global not-found handling.\n  - You can also add a `notFoundComponent` to any other route in your route tree to handle not-found errors for that specific route.\n- The `notFoundComponent` does not support rendering an `<Outlet>`.\n"}
